00:09:56.760 --> 00:09:58.050
We're gonna put this flavor back in there.

00:09:58.050 --> 00:09:59.343
- [John] Okay, all right.

00:09:59.690 --> 00:10:03.193
- [Yadi] Just get some regular
marinara, mix it all up.

00:10:03.450 --> 00:10:05.710
Now let's go ahead and
let's put some cheese on it.

00:10:05.710 --> 00:10:06.883
That's our Parmesan.

00:10:08.070 --> 00:10:10.513
Now we wanna go in with our mozzarella.

00:10:10.700 --> 00:10:11.870
Smells so good!

00:10:11.870 --> 00:10:13.970
Let's finish it with a little bit of salt.

00:10:16.940 --> 00:10:18.440
- Gosh, that is amazing.

00:10:18.440 --> 00:10:20.400
- So let's mix our cauliflower rice

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.253
and our mushroom-and-pea mix.

00:10:22.490 --> 00:10:25.610
That is the inside of our arancini balls.

00:10:25.610 --> 00:10:26.760
- Can you believe it's cauliflower?

00:10:26.760 --> 00:10:28.760
- I'm looking at it like cauliflower

00:10:28.760 --> 00:10:30.260
don't even exist in this dish.

00:10:30.260 --> 00:10:32.090
- [Yadi] We're gonna put
some smoked sweet paprika

00:10:32.090 --> 00:10:34.163
right into our Italian breadcrumbs.

00:10:35.880 --> 00:10:37.723
Take a nice, big old scoop in there.

00:10:38.680 --> 00:10:39.873
Perfect!

00:10:41.530 --> 00:10:43.680
Tam's gonna hook us up with some egg wash,

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:46.380
and then we're gonna get it
all up in our breadcrumbs.

00:10:49.400 --> 00:10:52.290
Remember how you thought
they were fried earlier?

00:10:52.290 --> 00:10:53.123
- Yes, yes, I did.

00:10:53.123 --> 00:10:55.133
- They're actually baked,
you're finding out.

00:10:55.180 --> 00:10:56.013
- Sorcery, man.

00:11:02.806 --> 00:11:05.350
- [Yadi] Then we're gonna
layer it with some pesto

00:11:05.350 --> 00:11:08.273
with a little bit of Parmesan
cheese, shiitake bacon,

00:11:08.460 --> 00:11:10.760
and then you're gonna
zest it with some lemon.

00:11:12.680 --> 00:11:15.413
- [Yadi!] Oooh!
- [Tam] Wow, that looks good.

00:11:20.250 --> 00:11:22.353
- It tastes almost like yours.
- Almost? What do you mean?

00:11:22.353 --> 00:11:23.500
- I think it's right on point.

00:11:23.500 --> 00:11:25.232
You got the crispiness, the crunchiness.

00:11:25.232 --> 00:11:26.065
- Honestly, this probably might be

00:11:26.065 --> 00:11:27.140
the only way she can ever
get me to eat cauliflower.

00:11:27.140 --> 00:11:29.100
- I think you did really, really well,

00:11:29.100 --> 00:11:31.463
and I'm very proud of you.
- I will cheers to that!

00:11:32.410 --> 00:11:34.460
Thank you for being game to try something

00:11:34.570 --> 00:11:35.620
you were totally afraid of.

00:11:35.620 --> 00:11:38.060
- Thank you for showing me a better way

00:11:38.230 --> 00:11:39.063
and a different path,

00:11:39.063 --> 00:11:40.970
'cause I would literally
walk out of here today

00:11:40.970 --> 00:11:44.430
with the same stigma that
cauliflower is disgusting.

00:11:44.430 --> 00:11:46.550
- Can I be so bold as to say

00:11:46.550 --> 00:11:49.320
that today's picky eater intervention

00:11:49.320 --> 00:11:51.473
actually worked?
- You have to say it worked.

00:11:51.473 --> 00:11:52.306
- It worked, it worked.

00:11:52.306 --> 00:11:54.533
- I guess a little Yadi dance.

00:11:54.594 --> 00:11:56.800
- You do a dance? Do
the dance, do the dance.

00:11:56.800 --> 00:11:59.570
- The champ is still here undefeated!

00:11:59.570 --> 00:12:02.283
Every vegetable you send my way, I slay!

00:12:02.320 --> 00:12:04.180
I don't think there's one
that can take me down.

00:12:04.180 --> 00:12:05.013
Chef Yadi's out!

00:12:06.554 --> 00:12:09.471
(triumphant music)

